<section id="faq">
<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

<FaqItem question="Can I really run a free AI chatbot on my website?">
<p>Yes. Tools like FastBots.ai and Chatbase offer genuinely functional free plans — not just time-limited trials. The free tiers include 1 chatbot, training on 1 source (a URL or text document), 25–30 messages per month, and a web widget for embedding. For low-traffic sites — personal blogs, portfolio sites, early-stage affiliate sites — the free plan is often sufficient indefinitely.</p>
</FaqItem>

<FaqItem question="What is the biggest limitation of free AI chatbots?">
<p>Message volume is the most common bottleneck — 25–30 messages per month runs out quickly on sites with moderate traffic. The more impactful limitation for affiliate marketers is the lack of lead capture integrations (email collection, CRM sync, meeting booking) on free plans. A chatbot that answers questions but cannot capture leads is leaving conversions on the table.</p>
</FaqItem>

<FaqItem question="When should I upgrade from free to paid?">
<p>Upgrade when you hit one of four triggers: (1) message limit exceeded consistently, (2) you want to add lead capture, (3) you need multiple chatbots for multiple sites, or (4) users are asking questions the bot cannot answer because of limited training sources. For most affiliate sites, trigger 2 (lead capture) or trigger 1 (message volume) drives the upgrade within the first 3–6 months.</p>
</FaqItem>

<FaqItem question="Which AI chatbot has the best free plan?">
<p>FastBots.ai offers 25 messages/month on the free tier, with good training quality from a single source. Chatbase offers 30 messages/month. For affiliate sites, FastBots is optimised for content-trained chatbots that answer reader questions. For business support use cases, Chatbase has stronger customer service features. Both are reviewed in detail on this site — see our <a href="/reviews/fastbots-ai-review/">FastBots review</a> and <a href="/reviews/chatbase-review/">Chatbase review</a>.</p>
</FaqItem>

<FaqItem question="Do AI chatbots actually improve affiliate conversions?">
<p>When configured for lead capture — not just Q&A — yes. A chatbot that answers product questions, captures the visitor's email address for follow-up, and recommends relevant content increases both time on site and lead capture rate. The improvement is most noticeable on product review pages where visitors have pre-purchase questions that the review text does not explicitly answer.</p>
</FaqItem>

<FaqItem question="Can I switch chatbot providers later without losing data?">
<p>Conversation history and training data are typically not portable between chatbot platforms. If you switch providers, you will need to re-train the new chatbot on your content and rebuild any custom behaviour rules. For this reason, starting with a tool that has a clear free-to-paid upgrade path (like FastBots or Chatbase) is preferable to starting on a free-only tool and migrating later.</p>
</FaqItem>
